{
  "summary": "Added Config import and changed session title from hardcoded 'nezha-agent-session' to dynamic `nezha-${agentId}` using Config.getInstance().getAgentId()",
  "learnings": [
    {
      "topic": "Test Coverage",
      "reminder": "When modifying any method that makes external calls (like fetch), always add/update tests to verify the request body and behavior"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Testing Pattern",
      "reminder": "Config.getInstance() calls need to be mocked in tests - check existing mocks in test files: vi.fn().mockReturnValue('test-agent-id')"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Code Review",
      "reminder": "Before committing changes, run test suite to ensure new code paths are covered"
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "No test coverage for doCreateSession method - the change to use getAgentId() is not verified by existing tests"
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "No validation if getAgentId() returns empty string - could result in odd session title 'nezha-'"
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    "Add test case for doCreateSession to verify the request body includes the agent ID",
    "Consider adding validation or fallback for getAgentId() returning empty string",
    "Add JSDoc comment explaining the session naming convention"
  ],
  "praise": "Good use of template literals instead of string concatenation. Consistent with existing codebase patterns (Config singleton). Good removal of hardcoded string in favor of dynamic value.",
  "scores": {
    "overall": 75,
    "codeQuality": 85,
    "testCoverage": 50,
    "documentation": 70
  }
}

